course: dictionary
lesson: 8725
title: A word that keeps things apart
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A separator is something that keeps two things apart, or splits one thing into parts. It can be a line, a wall or a sheet. «A bagless vacuum spins the air like a whirlwind, flinging dust to the sides of the bin where it drops; the idea came from big dust separators in sawmills.» The dust is flung to the sides and drops away from the air, so a separator here is a machine that splits the dust from the air.
explain: Use the swap check. Put a simple meaning like "thing that splits apart" into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. Clue words such as "divides", "apart", "splits" and "drops" all point to separating.
explain: In writing and maths, a separator is a mark, such as a comma, a slash, a space or a decimal point. It shows where one item ends and the next begins. In the number 3.5, the point is the separator between the whole part and the decimal part.
fact: A separator keeps two things apart, or divides one thing into parts.
fact: A separator can be a line, a wall, a sheet or a machine.
fact: «Dust separators» are machines that split dust from air in places like sawmills.
fact: In writing, a comma, a slash or a space can be a separator between items in a list.
fact: In maths, the point in 3.5 is a decimal separator, which divides the whole part from the decimal part.
exercise: In a list of fruit like «apple, pear, plum», what does the comma do? | *It shows where one item ends and the next begins | It is a kind of fruit | It means the list is finished forever | It makes the words louder
exercise: In the number 3.5, what does the point do? | It shows the number is negative | It means the number is a word | It makes the number bigger | *It splits the whole part from the decimal part
exercise: Which of these is a separator machine? | A torch that shines light | A pencil sharpener | A kettle that boils water | *A machine that splits cream from milk
test: In «the idea came from big dust separators in sawmills», what job do the separators do? | Heat the air | Make the sawmill louder | *Keep dust and air apart | Sell dust to farmers
test: Plastic sheets sit between biscuits in a packet. What is their job? | Hold the packet shut with glue | Biscuit crumbs for baking | Make the biscuits sweeter | *Keep the biscuits apart
exam: Which sentence best explains what a separator is? | *Something that keeps two things apart or splits one thing into parts | A word that means very old | A loud noise made by a machine | A kind of wet, grey weather
